+Neural graphics for FiveM (GTA V Legacy, 64-bit Windows), built to feel like a
+setting the game already had rather than a stack of mods.
+
+## For players
+
+Install it, start FiveM, press **Home**.
+
+```
+Look        Natural   Cinematic   Detail
+Strength    0.00 ──────── 1.00 ──────── 2.00
+Protect     Quality   Balanced   Performance
+Frames      Off    2x    3x
+```
+
+Strength 1.00 is not the middle of a range — it is the tuned point for the look
+you picked. Move away from it deliberately, not to "find" it.
+
+"Protect" is the one question that decides everything the software would
+otherwise have to guess: render resolution, how much frame time the pipeline may
+spend, and how quickly it gives detail up. On **Quality** the scene renders at
+full resolution, so the neural pass is antialiasing rather than reconstructing —
+the best-looking mode.
+
+That is the whole interface. Motion, depth, interface separation, which
+components load, how fast the game renders underneath a frame generator, and
+what to do when something breaks are all handled for you.
+
+### Installing
+
+Download the **built GitHub Actions artifact**, extract it completely, then double-click **`SECRET-EMKO.bat`**. Do not use GitHub **Code → Download ZIP** as the player installer: that archive contains source code and intentionally has no compiled add-ons.
+
+There is one installer and it works out what your machine can run. If you have a
+GeForce RTX 50 series card it installs the full neural stack; otherwise it
+installs the visual stack and tells you why. You can see exactly what it intends
+to do before it touches anything:
+
+```
+SECRET-EMKO.bat -WhatIf
+```
+
+To remove it, **`UNINSTALL.bat`**. It replays the install journal backwards and
+puts your machine back as it was, file by file.
+
+### Supply chain and downloads
+
+The player ZIP contains SECRET EMKO's compiled add-ons and the hash-pinned MIT-licensed DLSS5 Bridge. It deliberately does **not** hide third-party binaries inside encoded blobs.
+
+Before FiveM is modified, the installer prepares every external dependency in a temporary staging directory:
+
+- ReShade **6.8.0** is downloaded from `reshade.me` and checked against a pinned SHA-256. The full-add-on build is used only for Neural mode; Visual mode uses the standard build.
+- Shader packages are resolved from ReShade's public `EffectPackages.ini` catalog. Preset entries that are proprietary or absent from that catalog (for example QuantV files) are never fetched from unofficial mirrors. User-provided shader files are never deleted; techniques whose required file is unavailable in the prepared install are disabled in the installed preset.
+- Neural mode downloads the pinned RenoDX DLSS5 v4.70 provider and pinned DLSS NR/SR runtime archives, verifies the package hashes, and verifies the exact RenoDX and DLSS-NR binaries used by the live-control contract.
+
+Only after all of that succeeds does the journalled APPLY phase touch `FiveM.app\plugins`. A network or checksum failure therefore leaves the game installation unchanged.
+
+The compatibility bridge is installed but starts disabled. The runtime planner removes or adds its `DisabledAddons` entry for the **next** launch depending on whether Optical Flow / Hybrid motion is actually required. RenoDX and the input provider are controlled independently by the same policy.
+
+> Servers are allowed to forbid client plugins, and some do. This does not
+> bypass that, and no setting in it will.
+
+### Reading the status
+
+| Badge | What it means |
+|---|---|
+| `OFF` | you switched it off — strength is at zero |
+| `LOCKED` | it could work, but something it needs is not proven yet |
+| `READY` | everything is proven, nothing has been asked of it |
+| `ARMED` | configured, waiting for frames |
+| `ACTIVE` | frames are going through it **right now** |
+| `PAUSED` | running, deliberately suspended for a moment |
+| `BLOCKED` | a known failure, with the reason next to it |
+
+`ACTIVE` is earned, not assumed. A file being present, or a module being loaded,
+never produces it — and a claim that stops being re-proven drops back on its own
+within two seconds. If the Status page says `ARMED`, nothing is flowing, however
+good the frame counter looks.
+
+A `~` next to `ACTIVE` means the claim came from a component we do not own and
+could not be independently confirmed.
+
+### What works, and what does not
+
+The image pass runs. Motion for it is reconstructed from depth and the camera —
+exact for the world, approximate for traffic — with estimated motion filling in
+only where reprojection cannot see.
+
+Frame generation is locked, and this build will not unlock it.
+
+Generated frames need motion data derived from the game's geometry. GTA V does
+not produce any, so it has to be injected into the game's own shaders — that work
+is not done. Estimated motion from an optical-flow engine is **not** accepted as
+a substitute: it is what produces ghosting on fences and foliage, smeared
+vehicles and warped text.
+
+What does work today is the base-frame limiter, which is the part of frame
+generation that can be built and verified before the rest of it exists.
+
+---
+
+## For developers
+
+```
+src/core/     the entire decision layer — portable C++20, no Windows, no ReShade
+src/core/motion/  camera discovery, reprojection, motion validation — all tested
+shaders/      the compute passes, transcribed from src/core/ and checked against it
+src/app/      the orchestration loop and its two ports
+src/platform/ Windows facts, shared telemetry, configuration storage
+src/probe/    observers that deposit evidence
+src/effect/   actors that make a plan true
+src/ui/       ImGui, and nothing else
+src/fg/       the native input provider add-on
+tests/        298 assertions over the whole decision layer, runnable anywhere
+```
+
+### Building and testing the decision layer
+
+Needs nothing but a C++20 compiler. No GPU, no Windows, no SDK.
+
+```sh
+cmake -S . -B build && cmake --build build && ./build/emko_tests
+```
+
+```
+298 checks run, 0 failure(s)
+```
+
+That includes the parts most likely to be silently wrong: matrix inversion, the
+camera detector run against a synthetic drive with decoy matrices, and motion
+vectors checked against independently projected world points.
+
+Worth running before anything else: the rules of the product live in `core/`, and
+if they are wrong the Windows layer cannot save them.
+
+### Building the add-ons
+
+```powershell
+tools\build.ps1
+```
+
+Clones RenoDX, drops the sources in as two add-on targets, builds with MSVC, runs
+the core tests, verifies the export markers in the compiled binaries and stages a
+release with a manifest.
+
+### The one rule
+
+`core/` decides. `probe/` observes. `effect/` acts. `ui/` displays. Anything that
+looks like a decision outside `core/` is a bug — that separation is what makes
+the rules testable, and testable is what makes the status honest.
+
+See [`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) for the design and a frank
+list of what is verified and what is not, and [`docs/BUDGET.md`](docs/BUDGET.md)
+for what this costs in performance, latency and stability — including the
+latency that frame generation adds by construction and cannot give back.
+
+---
+
+## Built on
+
+- [ReShade](https://reshade.me/) add-on API — Patrick Mours / crosire, BSD-3-Clause
+- [RenoDX](https://github.com/clshortfuse/renodx) — Carlos Lopez Jr. and contributors, MIT
+- DLSS 5 Bridge — NIGos and contributors, MIT
+- NVIDIA DLSS and Streamline — NVIDIA, under NVIDIA's own terms
+
+The SECRET EMKO name covers this control layer only and implies no authorship of
+any of the above. See `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`.
+
+No PureDark code, binaries, authentication or paid assets are used.
+
+MIT licensed.
